- In this lab, we know the path to the admin panel which is "/admin" and we have to delete the user "Carlos.
- But we cannot perform action because we don't have admin rights. 
- Even after logging with default creds "wiener:peter", we don't see the option of admin panel.
- But in lab it is mention that "/admin" identify admin by a forgeable cookie.
- So will open the Burp suite and will intercept the traffic while we perform the logging function.

- In the Request tab, we will found that in "Cookie" field there are 2 parameter field
  - "Admin" and "Session"
- Now by default the Admin is "false".
- We will make it "True" and send the request. We will see that now the option of "Admin Panel" is visible of the user account.
- When we click on it, in the request tab again there is "Admin" field which is False, we will make it true.
- Now we entered the Admin Panel and can see the users : "Carlos" and "Wiener"
- Now if we try to delete them, it will again show that Admin is false by default in the request tab, again make it True.
- Because if don't make it you won't be able to delete the user, as every action require Admin Rights, from entering in the "Admin Panel" to "Deleting the user"
- Now delete the user and Your lab completed.

